=== (v) binary extended QR codes of length 8 and 24; Construction A of the Golay code ===
  p=7: 2 is a QR mod p: True (so the degree-(p-1)/2 factors of x^p-1 over F2 are the QR/NR generator polys); g = x^3 + x + 1
     extended QR code length 8: weight enumerator {0: 1, 4: 14, 8: 1}
  p=23: 2 is a QR mod p: True (so the degree-(p-1)/2 factors of x^p-1 over F2 are the QR/NR generator polys); g = x^11 + x^9 + x^7 + x^6 + x^5 + x + 1
     extended QR code length 24: weight enumerator {0: 1, 8: 759, 12: 2576, 16: 759, 24: 1}
  [8,4,4] with A4 = 14 is the extended Hamming code; [24,12,8] with 759/2576/759 is the extended Golay code (unique codes with these parameters)
  Construction A on extended Golay code: min nonzero weight 8 > 4, so norm-2 vectors are exactly the 48 vectors +-2e_i/sqrt2 -> root system A1^24; all weights = 0 mod 4 -> even; |C| = 2^12 -> det = 2^24/|C|^2 = 1 -> Niemeier lattice N(A1^24)

=== (vi) cannonball: sum_{k<=N} k^2 square for N <= 10^6 ===
  solutions: [(1, 1), (24, 70)]    sum_{k=0}^{24} k^2 = 4900 = 70^2 = 4900  => w = (0,1,...,24|70) has norm 4900 - 4900 = 0 in II_{25,1}

